  "activity": {
    "id": "act_dna_replication",
    "name": "DNA Structure and Semiconservative Replication",
    "description": "A hands-on AR lab guiding introductory molecular biology students from the schematic ladder representation of DNA through the double helix, antiparallel directionality, complementary base pairing, the enzymes of the replication fork, leading/lagging strand asymmetry, and the semiconservative nature of DNA replication.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_dna_replication",
    "start": "step_ladder",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step_ladder",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_model_stage",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1. The DNA Ladder: Backbones and Bases",
          "description": "Observe the flat, ladder-like DNA schematic. The two vertical rails are the sugar-phosphate backbones; each horizontal rung is a base pair made of two color-coded segments (adenine red, thymine blue, guanine yellow, cytosine green) labeled with one-letter abbreviations. Notice how the bases project inward from the backbone to pair with their complement on the opposite strand. When you are ready, say or click 'Next' to see the ladder become a real helix."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_ladder_schematic",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_intro"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_toggle_widget",
              "poi": "poi_helix_top"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "augmentation": "pred_ladder_schematic"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_intro"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_helix",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_helix",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_helix",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_model_stage",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2. From Ladder to Double Helix",
          "description": "Watch the ladder twist into the familiar double helix: the two backbones spiral around a common axis while the base pairs stack along the interior, completing about one full turn every ten base pairs. Use the toggle to switch between the schematic ladder and the realistic helix and build a mapping between the two. This is what DNA actually looks like inside your cells. Click or say 'Next' to explore strand direction."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_helix_realistic",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_toggle_widget",
              "poi": "poi_helix_top"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_helix"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_helix"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "augmentation": "pred_toggle_widget"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_antiparallel",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_antiparallel",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_antiparallel",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_model_stage",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3. Antiparallel Strands and 5'-to-3' Direction",
          "description": "Directional arrows now run along each backbone: one strand points up, the other down. Labels mark the 5' and 3' termini, which refer to carbon atoms of the sugar ring at each end of the backbone. The two strands always run in opposite directions \u2014 this antiparallel arrangement is forced by the directional chemistry of the sugar-phosphate backbone. Rotate the helix to confirm the arrows from any angle, then continue to the pairing activity."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_direction_arrows",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "primitive",
              "augmentation": "label",
              "poi": "poi_helix_top",
              "text": "5' end"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "primitive",
              "augmentation": "label",
              "poi": "poi_helix_bottom",
              "text": "3' end"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_antiparallel"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "augmentation": "pred_direction_arrows"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_model",
              "type": "primitive",
              "augmentation": "label"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_antiparallel"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_pairing",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_pairing",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_pairing",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_pairing_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "4. Build the Complementary Strand",
          "description": "A partial ladder shows a complete template strand (5'-ATGCCAGT-3') on the left and an empty backbone on the right. Drag loose bases from the palette to complete the complementary sequence. Correct pairings snap into place and form hydrogen bonds \u2014 two dashed lines for A-T, three for G-C; incorrect pairings are rejected with an explanation. Note that your new strand runs 3'-to-5', opposite the template, and that G-C pairs (three bonds) are stronger than A-T pairs (two bonds). Complete the strand, then click or say 'Next'."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_pairing_bench",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_partial_ladder",
              "poi": "poi_bench_template"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_base_palette",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_hbond_dashes",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_base_palette",
              "type": "primitive",
              "augmentation": "label",
              "poi": "poi_base_a",
              "text": "A"
            },
